{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":19064311,"ns":0,"title":"AC/DC receiver design","extract":"An AC/DC receiver design is a style of power supply of vacuum tube radio or television receivers that eliminated the bulky and expensive AC-only mains transformer. Having no mains transformer, receivers could operate from a DC supply as well as an AC supply (i.e., \"AC/DC\"), a feature which became less important as DC domestic electricity fell out of use.","description":"Type of power supply","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}